## Goal

Improve the PC presentation of the existing v1.1 art without replacing working atlases or touching gameplay. The current hero/monster/guardian assets are already distinct, but their small in-game render size and mostly geometric equipment accents leave the scene flatter than the source art deserves.

## Visual pass

- add a presentation-only `visual-polish.js` overlay;
- subtle class-colored player presence and skill-ready ring;
- restrained elite glow, stronger guardian presence, and a distinct final-boss pressure vignette;
- ten depth-band atmosphere tints so the 1→100 descent darkens and changes character instead of reading as one uniform canvas;
- sparse slow-moving dust for depth without obscuring grid readability;
- stronger town-scene contrast/depth plus clearer service-card separation;
- respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and cap overlay painting to about 30 FPS.

## Safety / scope

- no `game.js` changes;
- no hitbox, pathing, combat, RNG, save, economy, equipment stat, or input changes;
- no existing atlas is replaced in this pass;
- guardian telegraphs remain above the visual overlay and low-HP/minimap controls remain above both;
- the module is included in the static release allowlist and production script contract.

