Implements the first browser host from #129, stacked on the pure lane-governor core in #124.

## Browser boundary

- Manifest V3, Chrome 132+;
- zero requested permissions and zero host permissions;
- no `tabs` permission, content scripts, CDP/debugger, scripting, storage, cookies, history, network interception, screenshots, DOM reads, or provider adapter;
- browser-session lane projection uses numeric tab id only;
- popup renders numeric/fixed lifecycle metadata only: window/tab position/id, active, pinned, audible, discarded, frozen, auto-discardable, and governor decision/reason.

## Operations

The service worker imports the compiled #123 governor and uses browser-only application signals (`generating`/`unsaved` unknown, discard safety unknown), so absence of app knowledge never becomes an application-safe claim.

Operator actions:

- manual native discard: re-fetch tab, refuse active/pinned/audible/already-discarded/browser-protected state, then call `chrome.tabs.discard(tabId)`;
- wake: activate the tab and let Chromium reload discarded content normally;
- protect/unprotect: toggle `autoDiscardable` only.

All action responses are bounded lifecycle receipts with fixed failure/reason tokens. Browser errors are reduced to fixed local codes.

## Continuity

No storage is used. `chrome-session-tab-<tabId>` survives extension service-worker restart inside one browser session. Chrome tab ids are session-scoped, so this PR makes no browser-restart lane-identity claim.

